\DOC MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC

\TYPE {MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal asserting that a pair of states satisfies a {,,}-composed
{MAYCHANGE} relation, given an assumption asserting a smaller such relation for
the same two states.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. It applies to a goal {A ?- t} where {t} is a composition
via {,,} of {MAYCHANGE} components applied to two state terms, and {A} contains
an assumption of the same shape on the same two states. The assumption and the
conclusion may differ in the grouping, ordering and granularity of the
{MAYCHANGE} components (for instance individual components versus components
bundled into one list, or several narrow memory/register components versus one
wider one), with the conclusion covering at least as much as the assumption.
Other assumptions in {A} may be arbitrary and are neither used nor altered.
{
   A ?- t
   =================  MONOTONE_MAYCHANGE_TAC
                      (no subgoals)
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, only this closing behaviour on goals of this
{MAYCHANGE} form appears.

\ENDDOC
